{
  "_about": "Level of every LMS component in the design system (13 Oct 2026). Each LMS group page in Figma has one frame per level; after a rebuild with ds-group-page.js the blocks have to be split again with this map.",
  "_rule": [
    "Atom: one element with one job; nests no other LMS component. A thin wrapper around one base component (a badge, a button) is an atom too.",
    "Molecule: a few atoms and base components working as one unit; nests no other LMS molecule.",
    "Organism: a whole section of a screen, built from molecules and atoms.",
    "A level written at the start of a component description (Atom:, Molecule:, Organism:) wins.",
    "Judgement calls, not given by the rule: Course-Card and the player Topbar are organisms (as Program-Card and the platform Topbar); Course Detail / Topic-Row is a molecule although it nests Lock; Certificate and Course-Complete-Modal are organisms."
  ],
